<title>POLAND: C.BANK PICKS 17 POLISH MONEY MKT DEALERS FOR 1997.</title>
<headline>C.BANK PICKS 17 POLISH MONEY MKT DEALERS FOR 1997.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1996-12-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Polish central bank picked 17 banks as money market dealers for 1997 making only them eligible to participate in its open market operations next year, The National Bank of Poland said on Thursday.</p>
<p>The money market dealers will be allowed to participate in the NBP's open market operations and in primary NBP-bill tenders.</p>
<p>The banks activity have been evaluated in the July-November 1996 period.</p>
<p>A complete list of Polish money market dealers for 1997 (in alphabetical order) follows:  </p>
<p>1. Bank Gdanski SA</p>
<p>2. Bank Handlowy w Warszawie SA</p>
<p>3. Bank Inicjatyw Gospodarczych SA</p>
<p>4. Bank Ochrony Srodowiska SA</p>
<p>5. Bank Polska Kasa Opieki SA</p>
<p>6. Bank Przemyslowo-Handlowy SA</p>
<p>7. Bank Rozwoju Eksportu SA</p>
<p>8. Bank Slaski SA</p>
<p>9. Citibank SA</p>
<p>10.ING Bank Warsaw</p>
<p>11.Kredyt Bank SA</p>
<p>12.Polski Bank Inwestycyjny SA</p>
<p>13.Polski Bank Rozwoju SA</p>
<p>14.Powszechna Kasa Oszczednosci Bank Panstwowy</p>
<p>15.Raiffeisen-Centrobank SA</p>
<p>16.Societe Generale</p>
<p>17.Wielkopolski Bank Kredytowy SA</p>
<p>So far 29 banks primary dealers have played role of Polish</p>
<p>market makers under the individual deals signed with the NBP.</p>
<p>The NBP decided to extend the list to 17 banks from earlier</p>
<p>planned 15 because the rest of applicants was clearly behind</p>
<p>while the difference between 15th and 17th was small.</p>
<p>The minimum monthly average index of dealer's activity to</p>
<p>achieve a status of money market dealer was 21.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
